{
  "dom_id": "step-q68889",
  "name": "Question 2",
  "problem": "On a certain day in January, the temperature in New York in the morning was $-{2.4}^{∘}\\,\\text{C}.$ At noon, the temperature registered a slight increase of ${0.7}^{∘}\\,\\text{C}.$ What was the temperature in New York at noon?",
  "worked_solution": "To determine the temperature at noon, we add the variation in temperature to the temperature in the morning of that day This gives\n\n$$\n-{2.4}^{∘}\\,\\text{C}+{0.7}^{∘}\\,\\text{C}=-{1.7}^{∘}\\,\\text{C}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the temperature in New York at noon that day was $-{1.7}^{∘}\\,\\text{C}.$",
